  "question": {
    "text": "Young&rsquo;s modulus of elasticity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math>&nbsp;is expressed in terms of three derived quantities, namely, the gravitational constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi></math>, Planck&rsquo;s constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math> and the speed of light <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math>, as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msup><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></msup><msup><mi>G</mi><mi>&#947;</mi></msup></math>. Which of the following is the correct option?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "iUCvk",
